A_PROGRAM_CHECKED_ARTIFACT 87

This file is the canonical wire and authority manifest for the checked semantic
container implemented by `src/checker/container.c`. It is distinct from the
accepted proof artifact described by `artifact_v86.schema`.

The checked container transports untrusted semantic input. Reading it never
deserializes checked authority. The reader reconstructs an elaborated module,
validates its structure, and invokes the independent checker. Checked Context,
Substitution, occurrence, export, and module capabilities are process-local and
are never serialized.

All integers use little-endian byte order. U32 and I32 occupy four bytes; U64
and I64 occupy eight bytes. COUNT is U32 and may not exceed 16777216 while
reading. STRING is COUNT followed by that many bytes and has no trailing NUL on
the wire. ID fields are U32. The invalid ID is 4294967295.

header MAGIC VERSION SECTION_COUNT
MAGIC is the exact eight-byte sequence `APCHK087`.
VERSION is U32 and must equal 87.
SECTION_COUNT is U32 in 2..4.

section_kind SEMANTIC=1 CONTRACTS=2 PRODUCER=3 DEBUG=4
section KIND BYTE_COUNT FNV1A64 PAYLOAD

Every section begins with U32 KIND, U64 BYTE_COUNT, and U64 FNV1A64 followed by
exactly BYTE_COUNT payload bytes. FNV1A64 uses offset
1469598103934665603 and prime 1099511628211. A payload may not exceed
1073741824 bytes. Kinds outside 1..4, duplicate kinds, truncated payloads,
trailing file bytes, and hash mismatches are rejected.

SEMANTIC and CONTRACTS are required exactly once. PRODUCER and DEBUG are
optional and have no checked authority. The canonical writer emits SEMANTIC,
CONTRACTS, and then PRODUCER when a capsule is requested. The current writer
does not emit DEBUG. Readers do not derive authority from section order.

PRODUCER is an opaque work-capsule byte stream. Capsule extraction returns
producer work only and cannot mint a checked module. Removing PRODUCER or DEBUG
from an otherwise valid container does not change the semantic module checked
from SEMANTIC and CONTRACTS.

