The contracts payload has this exact field order:

contracts
  contracts
    KIND:I32 OCCURRENCE:ID CORE_TERM:ID COMPUTATION_OCCURRENCE:ID CONTINUATION_OCCURRENCE:ID CONTINUATION_BINDING_ID:U32 INPUT_CLASSIFIER:ID CLASSIFIER_FAMILY:ID EFFECT_ROW:ID EFFECT_CONSTRAINT_KIND:I32 NORMALIZATION_PROFILE:I32 SCHEMA_VERSION:U32
  dependencies OCCURRENCE:ID CONTRACT_ID:U32

Canonical ordering is defined by the checked semantic projection and checker
module, not by native C addresses or struct padding. Persistent codecs retain
the explicit order above and must not serialize native struct layouts.

The reader rejects malformed ranges and enum values through structural
validation before checking. It then reconstructs resource usage, Universe
constraints, classifier acceptance, interface validity, and runtime capability
requirements independently. Serialized assertions and optional sections are
not evidence for themselves.
